          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விரிப்பு — virippu — \"a bedspread; a sheet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அம்மா கட்டிலில் ஒரு புதிய விரிப்பை விரித்தாள். ammā kaṭṭilil oru putiya virippai virittāḷ. Mother spread a new sheet on the bed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It comes from விரி, to spread out; the noun and the verb often go together, as here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விரிப்பு (virippu) is native Dravidian, a noun made from விரி (viri), \"to spread out, to unfold\" (DEDR 5411), with the ending -ப்பு."
            }
          ]
        },
